# The birth of ⚡zap⚡

Or, why are the `log/slog` APIs so bizarre?

---

# Vibes in 2016

2016 was a different time.

- Microservices were new and trendy.
- Container orchestration was still unsolved.
- NoSQL and "big data" were crossing the chasm.
- OpenTelemetry and "observability" didn't exist.
- HTTP/2 hadn't been fully standardized.

---

# Go in 2016

In 2016, Go was *much* more immature.

- Go 1.6 had just been released.
- Rob Pike was leading the Go team.
- Russ Cox had *just* ported the compiler to Go.
- No dependency management: vendoring still feature-flagged.
- No context package.

---

# Uber in 2016

In 2016, Uber was 🍌bananapants🍌.

- All-in on microservices: >1 per engineer.
- Custom L7 network protocol.
- Custom service mesh implemented in Node.js.
- Controversial, bottoms-up Go adoption.

---

# Going fast

A small group of us was rebuilding the service mesh in Go, including the data
plane.

- The performance target was proxying 10k RPS/core...
- With p95 latency overhead of 1ms and p99 < 10ms...
- Which we hit...
- And then we tried to add some observability.

---

# logrus

```go
logger := logrus.New().WithFields(logrus.Fields{
  "host": "prod-sfo-123",
  "service": "winterfell",
  "pid": 1234,
})
logger.WithFields(logrus.Fields{
  "error": err,
  "code": 500,
  "caller": "horcrux",
  "request": myRequest,
  "metadata": metadata,
}).Error("oh no")

// ☠️ 11 µs, ~80 heap allocations
```

---

# logrus, under the hood

```go
type Fields map[string]any

type Logger struct {
  level uint32
  fields map[string]any
  
  mu sync.Mutex
  out io.Writer
}

func (l *Logger) WithFields(fs logrus.Fields) *Logger { ... }

func (l *Logger) Error(args ...any) { ... }
```

---

# Duplicate work

```
{"host": "prod-sfo-123", "service": "winterfell", "pid": 1234, "message": "oh no"}
{"host": "prod-sfo-123", "service": "winterfell", "pid": 1234, "message": "great success"}
{"host": "prod-sfo-123", "service": "winterfell", "pid": 1234, "message": "please"}
{"host": "prod-sfo-123", "service": "winterfell", "pid": 1234, "message": "help"}
```

---

# Allocations

```go
logger := logrus.New().
  WithFields(logrus.Fields{       // alloc map
    "host": "prod-sfo-123",       // alloc interface
    "service": "winterfell",      // alloc interface
    "pid": 1234,                  // alloc interface
  })                              // alloc map
logger.WithFields(logrus.Fields{  // alloc map
  "error": err,
  "code": 500,                    // alloc interface
  "caller": "horcrux",            // alloc interface
  "request": myRequest,
  "metadata": metadata,
}).Error("oh no")                 // alloc map + interface
```

---

# Lock contention

```go
if err != nil {
  logger.WithFields(logrus.Fields{"error": err}).Error(err.Error())
  return fmt.Errorf("XYZ: %v", err)
}
```

---

# Eager serialization

```go
type Fields map[string]any

type Logger struct {
  level   uint32
  message []byte
  // {"host": "prod-sfo-123", "service": "winterfell", "pid": 1234
  
  mu  sync.Mutex
  out io.Writer
}

func (l *Logger) WithFields(fs logrus.Fields) *Logger { ... }

func (l *Logger) Error(args ...any) { ... }
```

---

# Avoid interfaces

```go
type Field struct {
  key   string
  typ   uint32
  str   string
  num   int64
  iface any
}

type Logger struct { ... }

func (l *Logger) With(fs ...Field) *Logger { ... }

func (l *Logger) Error(fields ...Field)
```

---

# Sampling

```go
type Field struct { ... }

type Logger struct { ... }

func (l *Logger) With(fs ...Field) *Logger { ... }

func (l *Logger) Error(message string, fields ...Field)
```

```yaml
sampling:
  first: 100
  thereafter: 1000
```

